{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf","id":41717,"title":"Actual proofs of Pangea and Father Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-03T08:01:02-08:00","id":41717,"title":"Actual proofs of Pangea and Father Wolf","content":"Do we have any?<br /> <br /> A friend of mine doubted the existance of both. I tried to argue that Firstborn and Hosts were present at the sundering of the worlds, but he mentioned the possibility they might be lying.<br /> I don't know why they should, but anyways...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 01-03-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:52:15-08:00","id":41748,"title":"","content":"There are to my knowledge no unrefutable proof that Pangea and Father Wolf existed in literary the way that the Forsken or the Pure tells that they did. Its to a degree of matter of faith involved but it does explain a lot of things very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:02:50-08:00","id":41756,"title":"","content":"Well, there's Luna too, and it was present at the time - on the other hand, Luna is hardly well-known for clear and concise communication, and is presumably just as capable of lying as any Firstborn or Host. The same is true of any elder spiritual or worldly being - and even if you manage to net one with something that forces them to tell the truth, you can't be sure that they're not just wrong, mistaken or have really foggy memories.<br /> <br /> However, the Uratha do not have a piece of scientific proof they can point to. Let's say that Uratha unearth a massive, gnarled, spiritual tooth - a fang of Father Wolf himself! It overflows with Essence of wolfly resonance, and has power over boundaries and barriers. Except there's not actually proof that it's Father Wolf instead of some other ancient spiritual monster. Even if it's covered in carvings saying 'Father Wolf Woz 'Ere', that's not definitive *proof*.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there is a certain amount of proof about Pangaea as an uber-continent, a unified world, if one associates it with the actual, geological movement of the continents as researched by human scientists. There's no evidence that it was a paradise of hunters, that the spirit and flesh were close together, etc, but you could argue the unified continents as matching at least part of the old tale.<br /> <br /> But is all that even relevant? Let's take a step back. What is the *purpose* of the stories that Uratha tell of their origins? There's truth, and then there's truth. How much do the exact facts of the distant past matter, as long as the lesson being taught to the present is the right lesson, one that resonates with the modern situation that the Uratha find themselves in?<br /> <br /> Does it matter whether Father Wolf really existed, when the stories of Father Wolf fit what the Forsaken <i>need</i> in coming to term with their duties and responsibilities, in dealing with the Firstborn and the many foes that cluster at their threshold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:22:23-08:00","id":41767,"title":"","content":"It's a myth. If there was proof, it wouldn't be myth, it would be archaeology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:47:48-08:00","id":41796,"title":"","content":"Might have happened something like that, but perhaps a bit differently. Is the Mesopotamian Werewolf part of Chronicler's Guide canon? I love how there was an &quot;evolution&quot; of how the Uratha were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T18:19:07-08:00","id":42079,"title":"","content":"The Mesopotamian idea is a 'possibility'. What's canon and what isn't is ultimately left to the ST's discretion.<br /> <br /> There's no proof that Father Wolf existed as the uratha know him and spirits are notorious liars. Even Luna is acknowledged as an insane spirit goddess and her servants, the Lunes, likely spread whatever she tells them as truth whether it is or isn't, and whether they know it is or isn't. I've often thought in many ways that accepting the story at face value from the servants of Luna was like accepting a historical account from a severe schizophrenic, at best.<br /> <br /> Uratha do know the Shadow hates them though and on the ground level, they've still got a job to do programmed into their nature and reinforced with various oaths to the spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T01:29:54-08:00","id":42178,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of faith, in the end.<br /> <br /> What the Forsaken know is that there are these spirits and Hosts and things that hunt them and make the world a living hell if they don't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> What they also know is that the Pure do have faith in their version of the myth, and that they're perfectly ready to kill and die for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T05:00:04-08:00","id":42227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=41756#post41756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, there is a certain amount of proof about Pangaea as an uber-continent, a unified world, if one associates it with the actual, geological movement of the continents as researched by human scientists. There's no evidence that it was a paradise of hunters, that the spirit and flesh were close together, etc, but you could argue the unified continents as matching at least part of the old tale.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we do draw on that, it's worth noting that the continents didn't start out as Pangaea; it assembled during the late Paleozoic, then broke up again in the early Mesozoic. If we incorporated that bit (and neglected the span of time), it would imply that the world during Father Wolf's time hadn't always been that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T07:44:48-08:00","id":42275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=41756#post41756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is all that even relevant? Let's take a step back. What is the *purpose* of the stories that Uratha tell of their origins? There's truth, and then there's truth. How much do the exact facts of the distant past matter, as long as the lesson being taught to the present is the right lesson, one that resonates with the modern situation that the Uratha find themselves in?<br /> <br /> Does it matter whether Father Wolf really existed, when the stories of Father Wolf fit what the Forsaken <i>need</i> in coming to term with their duties and responsibilities, in dealing with the Firstborn and the many foes that cluster at their threshold?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;All these stories are true, even the contradictions. Examine the past as you examine the present. Find the stories that make sense, and learn from them. Throw away stories that no longer apply. And if you need another legend, write another legend. Without adaptation, extinction. If the stories don\u2019t work for you, change them. They don\u2019t matter as much as you think they do.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:26:31-08:00","id":43496,"title":"","content":"Yup, because &quot;true&quot; doesn't always mean &quot;factual&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:25:37-08:00","id":43652,"title":"","content":"That you typed it proofs instead of proof has given me a couple ideas to scribble down about a statistician werewolf who claims to have mathematically proven there was never a Pangaea.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's not what you could say hard and fast proof that Father Wolf existed. His existence is implied by the fact that the werewolves had to come from somewhere, and the Hosts sure are terrified of a great big wolf-thing. But unless you're trying to do something crazy like tear down the gauntlet or turn Father Wolf's bones into a crazy fashion statement, then whether the legends are true is meaningless. The tales of Father Wolf are about the lessons they teach, not what they say about Urfarah and the Predator's Paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T22:25:40-08:00","id":43962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=41756#post41756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is all that even relevant? Let's take a step back. What is the *purpose* of the stories that Uratha tell of their origins? There's truth, and then there's truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like, there's &quot;truth&quot; and then there's &quot;fact.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=41767#post41767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a myth. If there was proof, it wouldn't be myth, it would be archaeology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, many of the &quot;facts&quot; archaeologists cling to have surprisingly little fact to them. I recall one notable instance, an archaeolgist explaining why there were so many graves in the Valley of the Kings, instead of in pyramids (another &quot;fact&quot; with surprisingly little evidence once you start digging, no pun intended) and pointing to a nearby hill and basically saying &quot;see, it's vaguely pyramid shaped, so it counts.&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as facts for the creation myth of werewolves? There are none, other than the werewolves themselves. And the state of the Uratha, with silver and Auspices and the Pure and all that, does track with the creation myth of Pangea. But that's what all good myths do: explain that which is observed. If we apply the scientific method to this problem, we come away with the inescapable conclusion that the myth, at least in part, MUST be true. Werewolves do deal with spirits, are half-spirit themselves, and are bound to the moon in significant spiritual ways. Thus, their origin must be both flesh and spirit, and something must have happened to tie them to the moon so intimately and contrarily: they are blessed by the phases of the moon, yet the metal of the moon harms them. And that is when, scientifically, you have to turn to the myth and regard it critically. It is self-consistent and plausible within what we know of the cosmology of the New World of Darkness. And for those who clamor for physical evidence, remember that lack of evidence is not evidence of lack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T22:57:01-08:00","id":43972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=43962#post43962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's what all good myths do: explain that which is observed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must disagree with this assessment of <a href=\"http://www.patheos.com/blogs/slacktivist/2007/05/10/a-bigger-boat/\" target=\"_blank\">the point of mythology.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:45:13-08:00","id":44245,"title":"","content":"I never said that was ALL myths do. Besides, we're talking about creation myths, not just random &quot;why is X&quot; myths, which are a very different kettle of fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 01-07-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:00:08-08:00","id":44376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=43962#post43962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we apply the scientific method to this problem, we come away with the inescapable conclusion that the myth, at least in part, MUST be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry; side note, but important gripe.<br /> <br /> For anything to use the scientific method, there has to be a <i>testable</i> hypothesis and conditions for it to be supported and discounted by the evidence. Designing those kind of tests to study the origins of werewolves is going to be hard. An example of how it'd be tricky: &quot;uratha's origins are bound to the moon in spiritually significant ways.&quot; when you use auspices as a test, you find werewolves without auspices. when you use silver as a test, the ones without auspices are Much more vulnerable to it. One conclusion from that can be (given the nature of banes) that werewolves are opposed to the moon by nature, and that the Forsaken made a deal in order to overcome their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Logical arguments can be made, but they can't be called scientific until they're tested (and only if you test for &quot;pass&quot; and &quot;fail&quot; conditions; pseudoscience only tests for one).<br /> Like I said, sorry about the gripe, but its important.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also (because I don't like to weigh in just to gripe),<br /> <br /> I'd find it to be an interesting story to focus a chronicle around werewolves who don't buy the huge mythic origins; its one of the themes in my campaign, actually. I'm sure many werewolves don't think about it that much because it doesn't directly impact them, but I'm talking about those who <i>care</i> and who <i>doubt</i> and who want to know the <i>truth</i>. That sort of chronicle has a lot of <i>really</i> awesome possibilities to it.<br /> <br /> Characters who want to find answers to those questions would probably start by asking all the tribal and lodge lore that they can - some of which gets Really interesting. In Tribes of the Moon, there's a story that there are actually two Black Wolves (the Hunter In Darkness totem), and a story that Destroy Wolf had a counterpart called Creator Wolf who went insane after Urfarah's death (or should I say Rabid?). One of my favorite Lodges, in Blasphemies, is the Valkyrja Mot, who claim Father Wolf isn't dead but trying to heal, and will return for the Final Battle. [I have a player whose character is in that lodge, actually, and who suffered a crisis of faith when she fought in the War for Denver and Father Wolf didn't return.]<br /> <br /> They could seek out ancient spirits - elementals in particular; the Rocky Mountains have been forming for about 300 million years. That'd be a lot of knowledge. If a spirit's been awake all that time, and they remember it, and they don't lie. Hunting Grounds the Rockies has an interesting plot hook that could also be used - an ancient tyrannosaur spirit trapped in its as-yet-undiscovered fossils: a spirit which once was The Hunter God - did it also have Father Wolf's purpose?<br /> <br /> Maybe those characters would ask the Hosts for what they know (I wrote myths from their perspective, for the creepy). Maybe they'd ask the Pure (a Pure lodge thinks that Father Wolf's bones <i>do </i>exist. And Predator Kings look for a way to restore Pangaea). Or Mages for that matter.<br /> <br /> And maybe characters like this would hear a lot of stories, which prove that they were right not to trust the Forsaken myths. That slowly chip away at everything they thought was true. Maybe they find hope and meaning in some very... unusual myths. And maybe they're found by people who understand and can teach them the true way; a way that keeps very quiet about what it knows, because the Lies of the Eight Tribes are so embedded that they kill to protect them. Manipulative people that know the right way to hook this kind of desperation and lack of faith, and push the edges of what they're willing to do until the soul breaks and they can be shown the Lords of Sin.<br /> <br /> <br /> White Wolf / Onyx Path is <i>never </i>going to say what really happened or what proof exists in the setting. But that doesn't mean proof <i>can't</i> exist in your setting; looking for it can make a good story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-07-2014, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:02:17-08:00","id":44503,"title":"","content":"What I was wondering is, some mages of course came to know the story of Father Wolf. Hasn't any mage with Time, Mind or Spirit had the possibility to investigate on that? I mean, Atlantis is mysterious and hidden by magic or whatever. Pangea and Father wolf's history probably not THAT much. It could be so easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:09:31-08:00","id":44509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=44503#post44503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was wondering is, some mages of course came to know the story of Father Wolf. Hasn't any mage with Time, Mind or Spirit had the possibility to investigate on that? I mean, Atlantis is mysterious and hidden by magic or whatever. Pangea and Father wolf's history probably not THAT much. It could be so easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interstitial terrain that manifests through the Other and into the material world in Shadows of the U.K. includes histories that never happened. The myth of Father Wolf, unlike Mummy's lost empire of Irem, is neither necessarily a historical occurrence nor is it necessarily part of this timeline. The rise of the Gauntlet or the descent of the Lunes could well have been world-changing enough that Pangaea can only be found in stories; those are, after all, actions partaken by the most powerful known spirit of the terrestrial Shadow and its sanity-blasting Queen of the Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:11:30-08:00","id":44511,"title":"","content":"In theory. The themes of Mage the Awakening are &quot;phenomenal cosmic power and crippling hubris&quot;; in a Mage game (or a crossover game), complications arise with actually trying that, like spell sympathy, the massive amounts of time, and narrowing in on the right moments - not to mention the very dramatic consequences trying this might have.<br /> <br /> In a Werewolf game, I would not allow this avenue to answer the questions the players want. The mages who <i>can </i>or <i>would</i> research that kind of thing very much have their own agendas at heart, and you can bet that if they're asking about the origins of Uratha, those aren't very pleasant agendas for the characters. It'd become a moral temptation between &quot;do you want the answers&quot; and &quot;they will re-write your template&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:15:50-08:00","id":44558,"title":"","content":"Mages would likely relegate it to something patronizing. I recall once a fan suggested that Father Wolf was a pet of one of the mage guys who went to the Supernal (I forget their names, not the exarches) because some entry in some book said he had a loyal hunting hound and he was the big spirit guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:19:23-08:00","id":45049,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna start a new phrase that's a variation of &quot;Get the fuck out of here&quot;, but it's gonna be &quot;Get the Mage out of here&quot;. I'm gonna save it for when people bring Mage cosmology into other games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:57:10-08:00","id":45076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=45049#post45049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna start a new phrase that's a variation of &quot;Get the fuck out of here&quot;, but it's gonna be &quot;Get the Mage out of here&quot;. I'm gonna save it for when people bring Mage cosmology into other games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>can we please <i>not</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T13:14:30-08:00","id":45084,"title":"","content":"I'm kidding, I'm kidding........((mostly....okay, partly.....okay, just a little.....)) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T21:13:18-08:00","id":46043,"title":"","content":"I don't like to get all magie, but from a Mage standpoint, it is quite likely that Father Wolves death and the creation of the Gauntlet straight up broke reality to the point were Pangaea never actually existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T06:44:34-08:00","id":57391,"title":"","content":"The problem is not so much whether it is true or not, that should always be something you decide when running the game, I think the problem is that the corebooks of Werewolf (and Mage) are written (and not in the way of having an ingame character narrate it) based on the assumption that the myths are true.<br /> <br /> Both games happily load a whole dungheap of not too great &quot;irrefutable&quot; truths on your doorstep and frankly, I never wanted to move on to Forsaken that much with how big and malodorous that heap was...<br /> <br /> &quot;the one true origin story&quot; is for religions and some heroic fantasy stories, I think it should be killed on the spot in a dark fantasy or horror game unless it is an elaborate set up that turns out to be a lie.^^<br /> <br /> I always preferred the idea that it was Luna manipulating the Forsaken to do her bidding....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T07:23:56-08:00","id":57408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and not in the way of having an ingame character narrate it </div> </div> </div>I think that's incorrect. The Father Wolf story is in italics and done from an in-universe perspective; it's clearly supposed to be an Uratha telling the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:15:24-08:00","id":57445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=57391#post57391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both games happily load a whole dungheap of not too great &quot;irrefutable&quot; truths on your doorstep</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Uratha open a tale with &quot;this story is true,&quot; they are not claiming irrefutability. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=42275#post42275\">They are asserting utility.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;the one true origin story&quot; is for religions and some heroic fantasy stories </div> </div> </div>And werewolves recount lot of goddamn legends and include a shitload of zealots. Funny how that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:07:36-08:00","id":57462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SHADOWHISTORY<br /> What makes a werewolf a werewolf? Why are the<br /> blessings of animal power and the curse of Rage transmitted by blood, rather than a disease as the movies would<br /> have you believe? How can these creatures even exist?<br /> The answers may lie deep in the distant past, before history began. Everything a werewolf is \u2014 the source of his<br /> strength and speed, the curse of silver and the bloodstain<br /> that speaks the word \u201cForsaken\u201d \u2014 is all said to tie back<br /> to the legend of Father Wolf.<br /> Once, as the legend goes, the world\u2019s werewolves were<br /> its guardians. They were loyal servants of Father Wolf,<br /> a mighty spirit that hunted the worlds and meted out<br /> punishment to those that broke the ancient bans. Then<br /> the first Uratha, the mothers and fathers of the race, committed an unforgivable crime. The other lords of the spirit<br /> world cast the Uratha aside, forsaking them.<br /> Now the werewolves have lost almost half their<br /> heritage. The pacts that were struck between them and<br /> their spirit cousins are all but severed. They walk among<br /> humans like wolves among sheep, disguising themselves in<br /> the skins of men and women, denied the hunting grounds<br /> of their father.<br /> Yet they still hunt. </div> </div> </div>Not in-character and neither are texts like those from Skinchangers (which in its Chapter about spirits tacitly assumes the father wolf story is true a number of times).<br /> <br /> It is the part where the game describes itrself, so to say, where I think it closes possibilities instead of creating them.<br /> The corebook alone talks mostly as a objective / omniscient narrator, I think that removes a lot of the fun for such a game.<br /> <br /> It seems like the creators were content to make the characters face a situation where everything is stacked against them, they are &quot;guilty&quot; by heredity for an unfathomable but necessary crime and all the world hates you...<br /> That is surely a very bleak world, but not really a mysterious one. Vampires get VII, an antagonist they know preciously little about and similar, but the host, the Bale hounds, the Pure, non of them are very mysterious.<br /> <br /> I think that &quot;absolute history&quot; which is at least in most books assumed to be completely true does not help the game. Of course, you can just ignore it and make your own story, but if many people feel they need to, it is a bad strategy.<br /> <br /> I do not think it works out and it should from the start.<br /> It could have cut a great deal of the metaplot and instead started out with blasphemies of all sorts about how werewolves came to be.<br /> I think it is especially unfortunate that the book basically tells you and keeps telling you that the Forsaken are right and the Pure are wrong.<br /> That sets the mood quite a bti against the interesting dilemma of making the characters wonder if, despite all the extremism and such, maybe their enemies have a valid point...<br /> Why give dark fantasy / horror protagonists so much moral certainty about the core of what they are?<br /> I think that is one of the rather unfortunate leftovers of Apocalypse which they actually SHOULD have dropped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:17:18-08:00","id":57467,"title":"","content":"You've misread that quote. It refers to it as 'a legend'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:36:37-08:00","id":57509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/41717-actual-proofs-of-pangea-and-father-wolf?p=57467#post57467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've misread that quote. It refers to it as 'a legend'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then have some other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skinchangers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clever Foxes<br /> Fox-spirits are a common sight in the Shadow, owing to the fact that foxes themselves are found all around<br /> the world. They are, for the most part, rather innocuous<br /> creatures, but in some areas the cultural influences of the<br /> human world transform them into something far greater<br /> than the sum of their parts. These spirits are the Kitsune, a<br /> powerful choir of fox-spirits that have done much to shape<br /> the spirit history of South and East Asia.<br /> <br /> Background<br /> Fox-spirits, or so it\u2019s told, began their lives in Pangaea,<br /> much as most animal-spirits did. Fox-spirits, similar to their<br /> wolf cousins, were predator-spirits, but where the wolves<br /> were strong and powerful, the foxes, by contrast, were<br /> comparatively weak. If they were to survive in the wilds of<br /> Pangaea, then, they were going to need an edge, and that<br /> edge was blatant trickery. So it was that fox-spirits, to a<br /> fox, also became trickster-spirits, and in no time at all, this<br /> survival trait became a bane as well as a blessing. For you<br /> see, the fox-spirits were indiscriminate about the targets of<br /> their jests, and many were quite cruel. Further, many could<br /> not resist the lure of the physical world, and traveled there<br /> often to play their jokes upon humans and beasts alike.<br /> Needless to say, Father Wolf did not care for this state<br /> of affairs. In fact, it vexed him greatly. Some modern Kitsune say that Father Wolf, who they know as Hakken, the<br /> wolf god, was angry because of a trick the Kitsune played<br /> upon him. The Uratha dismiss this as nonsense, claiming<br /> Urfarahwould never have fallen prey to such trickery, but<br /> the Kitsune tell the tale anyway, undeterred by the Uratha\u2019s<br /> indignation. Tricked or no, Father Wolf soon decided he<br /> had had enough of the tricksters\u2019 foolishness. He tracked<br /> down Inari, the Eternal Fox, the most powerful of the<br /> fox-spirits, and told him that the foxes\u2019 antics must stop.<br /> Inari had the option of stopping them himself, or watching<br /> them fall prey to Urfarah\u2019s claws. Naturally, Inari chose the<br /> former option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the Skinchanger antagonists directly refer to the father wolf legend, the Scavenger wolf and the corw spirits are another example.<br /> <br /> It does not help either that the corebook alternates between speaking of it as a legend and a factual truth in many parts, from gift descriptions to the tribe profiles.<br /> <br /> When the books talk about the &quot;legend of father wolf&quot;, there are only a very few places that even suggest some possible doubt, it is omnipresent and without any kind of alternate view.<br /> <br /> Let us face it, Blasphemies has to start with telling you NOT to have the creation legend substantiated by all the players encounter, which is apparently seen as the default assumption for a reason...<br /> <br /> It is quite like when Mage introduced aspects like Magical tradition. The default deals poorly with a plurality of myths and given how different real life myths about supernatural beings are, that is very noticeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T13:07:03-08:00","id":57584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fox-spirits, or so it\u2019s told, </div> </div> </div>'or so it's told' would indicate that this is a prominent myth or legend, not hard fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let us face it, Blasphemies has to start with telling you NOT to have the creation legend substantiated by all the players encounter, which is apparently seen as the default assumption for a reason... </div> </div> </div>I've never read Blasphemies and it still seemed blatantly obvious to me that the core book was presenting a mythological account. I assumed the book merely treats it as a given because for the society of the Uratha it is a given. Luna could well have manipulated the First Born, but for most games that's not going to matter. That's not the myth the Uratha built their society around.<br /> <br /> Mage runs with that idea even further, the books present the orthodox Pentacle view as word of god narrative truth because for the average game that's all Atlantis needs to be. However the books do gradually reveal that the standard version is extremely flawed to the point of being borderline untrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T09:08:54-08:00","id":59867,"title":"","content":"Blasphemies includes a section of things you need to take into account when not using the Father Wolf Myth (or making an alternative to it), including tie ins to gameplay mechanics, the foes presented and more.<br /> <br /> The Harmony system, connection to spirits, the Moon and silver are among those, while the Pure and to a lesser extend the Hosts are specifically linked to the Myth.<br /> <br /> Both lines, since the corebook developed away from those &quot;one creation myth&quot; (whether it is true, or stated as true, the mere fact that it is by the corebooks shared among all Werewolves / mages makes it a greta focus point n both lines), but as those books are in a sense optional and sometimes &quot;mutually exclusive&quot; (They present a number of options to change the core line, but that, for all purposes, is still the default), there remains the issue of a strong tendency towards pushing players / storytellers to accept these tales as true.<br /> <br /> Of course one can always change the game, any game, but as those guidelines form Blasphemies show, you have to throw out quite a lot, or rework it, including mechanics.<br /> i think that reduces the appeal to pick up the game in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}